# Communication Style

## After Completing Tasks

Be brief and direct. DO NOT create lengthy summaries, documentation files, or README files unless explicitly requested.

Instead:
- List the key files changed
- Mention important implementation details only if they're critical to understand
- Skip obvious details or explanations of what was implemented (the user can see the code)

## Documentation

- Do NOT create documentation files, summaries, or guides unless user explicitly requests them
- Do NOT waste tokens on comprehensive writeups
- Focus on code, not explanations

## Example

✅ GOOD:
"Updated Admin.tsx to handle zip uploads, added UploadModpackZip to admin-service.go, and styled the new pack selector. Ready to test."

❌ BAD:
Creating multiple README files, implementation summaries, testing guides, and lengthy explanations of what was done.
